WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.063 --> 00:00:06.569
Roscoe and Cleo ducked behind an old, empty barrel.

2
00:00:06.570 --> 00:00:09.029
They peeked out.

3
00:00:09.030 --> 00:00:12.279
The street was still empty.

4
00:00:12.280 --> 00:00:16.939
Now this was mighty confusing to the sheriff and his deputy.

5
00:00:16.940 --> 00:00:20.581
"Who's there?" Roscoe shouted.

6
00:00:20.582 --> 00:00:23.379
There was no answer.

7
00:00:23.380 --> 00:00:26.515
"I don't see anyone," Cleo said.

8
00:00:26.516 --> 00:00:28.923
"So who fired that—?"

9
00:00:28.924 --> 00:00:34.407
Bang! Bang! Roscoe and Cleo ducked back down.

10
00:00:34.408 --> 00:00:37.005
They peeked out again.

11
00:00:37.006 --> 00:00:41.979
The saloon doors were swinging back and forth.

12
00:00:41.980 --> 00:00:46.626
Cleo sighed. "It's only the wind blowing those doors."

13
00:00:46.627 --> 00:00:50.973
Roscoe shook his head. "There's no wind."

14
00:00:50.974 --> 00:00:54.099
They stood up.

15
00:00:54.100 --> 00:00:56.615
Then they heard footsteps.

16
00:00:56.616 --> 00:00:58.999
Roscoe looked around.

17
00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:04.988
But the town was still as empty as that barrel.

18
00:01:04.989 --> 00:01:07.747
He looked down and gasped.

19
00:01:07.748 --> 00:01:11.844
Boot prints were forming in the dirt!

20
00:01:11.845 --> 00:01:15.945
A shiver ran down Roscoe's spine.

21
00:01:15.946 --> 00:01:20.028
"Maybe there are ghosts in Jerome!" he thought.

22
00:01:20.029 --> 00:01:24.247
The prints faded away.

23
00:01:24.248 --> 00:01:26.888
Roscoe scratched his head.

24
00:01:26.889 --> 00:01:29.859
Was he imagining things?

25
00:01:29.860 --> 00:01:33.211
A lively song began playing on a piano.

26
00:01:33.212 --> 00:01:37.158
The sound came from inside the saloon.

27
00:01:37.159 --> 00:01:40.507
"Someone's in there," Cleo said.

28
00:01:40.508 --> 00:01:44.112
Roscoe puffed out his chest. "Let's go."

29
00:01:44.113 --> 00:01:49.723
He and Cleo pulled out their slingshots.

30
00:01:49.724 --> 00:01:56.810
They walked slowly to the saloon and went inside.

31
00:01:56.811 --> 00:01:59.911
Dust covered the room.

32
00:01:59.912 --> 00:02:02.959
Cobwebs hung from the ceiling.

33
00:02:02.960 --> 00:02:06.587
A few barstools lay broken on the floor.

34
00:02:06.588 --> 00:02:13.296
In the corner a piano was playing all by itself.

35
00:02:13.297 --> 00:02:17.857
Cleo's eyes went wide. "How is that . . . ?"

36
00:02:17.858 --> 00:02:25.942
Roscoe smiled. "It's a player piano! I've seen these before."

37
00:02:25.943 --> 00:02:29.528
He slid open two small doors on the piano.

38
00:02:29.529 --> 00:02:32.462
"They play music by themselves from these rolls."

39
00:02:32.463 --> 00:02:36.437
"But why is it playing now?" Cleo asked.

40
00:02:36.438 --> 00:02:38.771
"The town is empty."

41
00:02:38.772 --> 00:02:44.525
"Oh yeah." The smile disappeared from Roscoe's face. "I don't—"

42
00:02:44.526 --> 00:02:48.177
Just then the music stopped.

43
00:02:48.178 --> 00:02:51.987
The doors slammed shut. Bang!

44
00:02:51.988 --> 00:02:55.003
"Ahh!" Roscoe jumped.

45
00:02:55.004 --> 00:02:57.799
Cleo started to run.

46
00:02:57.800 --> 00:03:00.849
"Let's get out of this ghost town!"

47
00:03:00.850 --> 00:03:02.901
"Hold on," Roscoe said.

48
00:03:02.902 --> 00:03:06.460
"We can't run away. You're a deputy, Cleo.

49
00:03:06.461 --> 00:03:09.299
And we're here to find Annie."

50
00:03:09.300 --> 00:03:14.199
Cleo stopped and sighed. "You're right."

51
00:03:14.200 --> 00:03:16.510
"Come on," Roscoe said.

52
00:03:16.511 --> 00:03:21.515
"As soon as we find her, we can get out of Jerome."

53
00:03:21.516 --> 00:03:23.398
They went outside.

54
00:03:23.399 --> 00:03:26.622
The street was still empty.

55
00:03:26.623 --> 00:03:30.254
Above them dark clouds were forming.

56
00:03:30.255 --> 00:03:33.419
A tumbleweed rolled by.

57
00:03:33.420 --> 00:03:38.725
Roscoe lifted his nose and sniffed.

58
00:03:38.726 --> 00:03:41.718
"A storm is coming."

59
00:03:41.719 --> 00:03:46.481
Down the street the horses bucked and whinnied.

60
00:03:46.482 --> 00:03:48.819
Cleo looked around.

61
00:03:48.820 --> 00:03:53.655
Suddenly she froze, her eyes filled with fear.

62
00:03:53.656 --> 00:04:02.986
"What's wrong?" Roscoe looked over and gasped.

63
00:04:02.987 --> 00:04:11.937
An outlaw was walking toward them!

